<div class="help-faq" id="faq">
<h2 class="help-faq__heading-frequently-asked-questions">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<p class="help-faq__text">Having problems when searching for items across the cultural collections? Here are some frequently asked questions to help.</p>
<h3 class="help-faq__question">How do I search across multiple collections at once?</h3>
<p class="help-faq__answer">By default, searches run across every collection in Cultural Collections Search. Use the filters on the results page to narrow a single collection, or to further refine your results by object type, access condition, or date.</p>
<h3 class="help-faq__question">What collections are currently included?</h3>
<p class="help-faq__answer">The platform is continuously being improved to include items from across the University's museums, archives, art, and scientific collections. Use Browse Collections to see the contributing collections. Please revisit frequently to discover new added items and collections.</p>
<h3 class="help-faq__question">Can I download images from my search results?</h3>
<p class="help-faq__answer">It depends on the item's copyright and terms of use. If a download icon appears near the preview window, you know the image, audio, or video can be used non-commercially. Respectful of the terms of use by always attributing the creator and the University of Melbourne.</p>
<h3 class="help-faq__question">How do I request digital access to a collection item?</h3>
<p class="help-faq__answer">Contact the Collection Team for digital access. It makes the process easier if you include the item's persistent identifier and a description of your intended use.</p>
<h3 class="help-faq__question">How do I report any incorrect or incomplete metadata?</h3>
<p class="help-faq__answer">We welcome community knowledge to help improve the accuracy of our records. Contact the Collection Team and include the item's persistent identifier to make the process easier.</p>
<h3 class="help-faq__question">What can I do if I have problems accessing the search?</h3>
<p class="help-faq__answer">Try clearing your cache in the browser you are using. Browsers often save outdated information, which is the most common cause of access errors. Here is more information on how to clear your cache on PC or Mac.</p>
<h3 class="help-faq__question">What can I do when there is a broken link on the website</h3>
<p class="help-faq__answer">If you come across a link that is not working or has taken you somewhere unexpected, retrace your steps from the homepage.</p>
<h3 class="help-faq__question">When all else fails …</h3>
<p class="help-faq__answer">Contact us. To help us fix your problem as quickly as possible, describe the exact steps you took to get the error, and remember, screenshots are worth a thousand words.</p>
</div><aside aria-labelledby="h-contact-box-topic" class="contact-box">
